"[Samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic/) to create annotated "
"boxes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Convert the options {#step-3-convert-the-options}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most [`NoiseLearnerOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-noise-learner-options) fields map directly to "
"[`NoiseLearnerV3Options`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-models-noise-learner-v3-options), except the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`max_layers_to_learn`: With `NoiseLearnerV3`, the number of layers to learn "
"is based on the number of layers passed in.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`twirling_strategy`: With `NoiseLearnerV3`, the twirling strategy is defined"
" by how the instructions are boxed and annotated (such as when using "
"`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are planning to use client-side Estimator for circuit execution, you can\n"
"set the `twirling.strategy` Estimator option:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are planning to use Executor for circuit execution, you can pass the "
"`twirling_strategy` option to the "
"[generate_boxing_pass_manager](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-"
"generate-boxing-pass-"
"manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager) function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that with `generate_boxing_pass_manager()`, the `twirling_strategy` values use underscores\n"
"(`\"active_accum\"`, `\"active_circuit\"`), whereas `NoiseLearnerOptions.twirling_strategy` values use hyphens (`\"active-accum\"`, `\"active-circuit\"`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Inspect the results {#step-4-inspect-the-results}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The outputs of `NoiseLearner` and `NoiseLearnerV3` contain similar "
"information but are in different formats. Update your code if it inspects "
"the output explicitly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Result attribute mapping:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "(`learner_result` is the output of the learner job)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Attribute | NoiseLearner | NoiseLearnerV3 |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Result type | [NoiseLearnerResult](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-result#noiselearnerresult) | [NoiseLearnerV3Results](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-v3-results), a sequence-like container of [NoiseLearnerV3Result](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-v3-result) |\n"
"| Number of learned layers | len(learner_result.data) | len(learner_result) |\n"
"| Data for the first layer | layer_error = learner_result.data[0] | noise_map = learner_result[0].to_pauli_lindblad_map() |\n"
"| Result type of each layer | [`LayerError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-layer-error) (`type(layer_error)`) | [`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) (`type(noise_map)`) |\n"
"| Generators for the error channel | `layer_error.error.generators` | `noise_map.generators()` |\n"
"| Error rates | `layer_error.error.rates` | `noise_map.rates` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 5: Input noise model to a primitive {#step-5-input-noise-model-to-a-"
"primitive}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NoiseLearner` only works with the legacy server-side `Estimator`, and "
"`NoiseLearnerV3` only works with `Executor` and the client-side `Estimator`."
" How a noise model is specified varies slightly based on which primitive is "
"used.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`NoiseLearner`, when working with legacy server-side Estimator:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reuse the same `Estimator` that produced `layers` in step 2. The noise maps returned by the\n"
"learner are positionally matched to those layers, so they must be assigned to the Estimator\n"
"they came from. PEA/PEC was already enabled on it in step 2.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that while `NoiseLearnerV3` supports both Pauli-Lindblad and TREX "
"protocols, `Estimator` only accepts noise models for two-qubit layers "
"learned with the Pauli-Lindblad protocol.\n"
msgstr ""

